= What does it feel like to be Alienated?
Imagine being in a room full of people. Or on a family dinner table with your
parents. They are sitting right there, and yet they can't _see_ you. Whatever
you say to them they can't _hear_ you because they are thinking about something
else. Or being with yourself and yet you can't feel joy alone! You go on your
phone trying to numb the feelings of being unseen. Unheard. Invisible. Or you
work and work and work, and yet you can not derive the joy from work because
you are alienated from it! You don't
care about the work you are doing. It sucks away your soul. You have no joy in
your heart. If you've ever had the chance to read _Invisible Man_ - it is that
feeling that I'm trying to evoke in you.

== Alienated from those around you
My mother always says she loves me but she never _saw_ me. She projected an
image of what she wanted me to be, her anxieties, her anger, her guilt, her
shame,  _onto me_ and then say that what I did was wrong! She always wanted me
to be some monk, some politician, or save the world in some way, without really
considering how _I_ was feeling. I felt like a robot to her, and I refused to
be a robot. 

She loved me, sure. She also took care of me for some moments. She
fed me, clothed me, did her best for me. Made sure I get good education by
moving me to America to be with my Grandmother. She would try to visit and
connect with me. But because of the darkness in her heart, the anger, the
shame, the guilt, I could not _recieve_ her love. No matter how hard she tried,
the dark moments in her meant that it also clouded me from recieving her love.

